course: dictionary
lesson: 6616
title: Finding northwest
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Northwest is one of the compass points on a map. It lies halfway between north and west. On most maps north is at the top and west is on the left, so northwest is the direction up and to the left.
explain: Northwest can name a direction, a place, or something that faces that way. «About 4,500 years ago great cities stood by the river Indus, in today's Pakistan and northwest India.» Here northwest means the northwest part of India.
explain: Capital letters show a special name. «Roald Amundsen first sailed the Northwest Passage between 1903 and 1906.» The Northwest Passage is a sea route through the Arctic, north of Canada. A wind that blows from the northwest is a northwest wind.
fact: Northwest is written NW on maps and weather reports.
fact: The eight compass points are north, northeast, east, southeast, south, southwest, west and northwest.
fact: The Northwest Passage is a sea route through the Arctic, north of Canada.
fact: The Pacific Northwest is a region of the USA and Canada.
fact: You may see the phrases to the northwest, in the northwest and north-west of.
exercise: On a map, which direction is halfway between north and west? | East | *Northwest | Northeast | Southwest
exercise: «About 4,500 years ago great cities stood by the river Indus, in today's Pakistan and northwest India.» What is northwest in this sentence? | A sea route | *A part of a country or area | A wind | A kind of feast
exercise: Which one is a northwest wind? | *A wind that blows from the northwest | A wind that blows from the south | A wind that blows across the sea at night | A wind that blows from the east
test: What does NW stand for on a map? | Narrow Way | Northern World | *Northwest | Northeast
test: Which name is a sea route through the Arctic, north of Canada? | *The Northwest Passage | Northwest wind | To the northwest | The Pacific Northwest
exam: In the sentence «On the Pacific Northwest Coast of Canada, chiefs won respect by giving huge gifts», what is the Pacific Northwest? | *A region of the USA and Canada | A type of wind | A sea route in the Arctic | A kind of food
